-- Cases for the Cat Act 2011 (WA) Parts 1-2, the Cat Regulations 2012 provisions they depend on,
-- and Interpretation Act 1984 ss 61, 62, 71, 72. LQA run cat-act-2011-lqa, step 4A, 2026-10-01.
-- Every person, cat and company below is invented. The holiday list is illustrative: which days
-- are public holidays is a fact the Act leaves to other law (IA s 61(2)).
-- Where a fork divides two readings, both are asserted on the facts that divide them; the
-- assertion of the reading NOT taken is marked "reading B".

§ `Fixtures`

`the holidays` MEANS LIST `the date` 2026 12 25, `the date` 2026 12 28, `the date` 2027 1 1, `the date` 2027 1 26

`no holidays` MEANS LIST `the date` 1970 1 1

GIVEN n IS A STRING, born IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Person`
`an adult` n born MEANS `Person` WITH
    `name`                            IS n
    `date of birth`                   IS born
    `parents or guardians`            IS EMPTY
    `became resident in the State on` IS JUST (`the date` 2000 1 1)
    `convictions`                     IS EMPTY
    `is a veterinarian`               IS FALSE
    `is a veterinary nurse`           IS FALSE
    `units of competency completed`   IS EMPTY
    `courses completed`               IS EMPTY
    `is an approved cat breeder`      IS FALSE
    `is an eligible pensioner`        IS FALSE

