    `keeps a microchip database` IS TRUE
    `keeps, or has agreed to keep, records about the cat and its owner` IS TRUE

GIVEN who IS A `Person`, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH AN `Implant`
`a compliant chip implanted by` who `on` d MEANS `Implant` WITH
    `device complies with AS 5018-2001 and AS 5019-2001` IS TRUE
    `device is capable of being implanted in a cat` IS TRUE
    `device is designed to record information that can be electronically retrieved` IS TRUE
    `implanted by` IS who
    `implanted on` IS d

GIVEN who IS A `Person`, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Sterilisation`
`a desexing by` who `on` d MEANS `Sterilisation` WITH
    `made permanently infertile` IS TRUE, `by a surgical procedure` IS TRUE
    `performed by` IS who, `performed on` IS d

GIVEN lg IS A STRING, n IS A STRING, p IS A `Period of registration`, e IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Registration`
`a registration with` lg `in the name of` n `for` p `from` e MEANS `Registration` WITH
    `with local government` IS lg, `in the name of` IS n, `registration number` IS "R-1"
    `registered for` IS p, `has effect from` IS e, `cancelled on` IS NOTHING, `recorded in the register` IS TRUE

-- A cat, with the facts most cases vary as arguments and the rest at ordinary values.
GIVEN n IS A STRING
      born IS A `Calendar date`
      ks IS A LIST OF `Keeper`
      rs IS A LIST OF `Registration`
      imp IS A MAYBE `Implant`
      st IS A MAYBE `Sterilisation`
GIVETH A `Cat`
`a cat` n born ks rs imp st MEANS `Cat` WITH
    `cat name`                                               IS n
    `is an animal of the species felis catus or a hybrid of that species` IS TRUE
    `born on`                                                IS born
    `keepers`                                                IS ks
    `ordinarily kept in the district of`                     IS "City of Perth"
    `is kept in the State`                                   IS TRUE
    `has died`                                               IS FALSE
    `registrations`                                          IS rs
    `implant`                                                IS imp
    `microchip database company`                             IS JUST `Petsafe`
    `name recorded as owner in a microchip database`         IS NOTHING
    `there is evidence to the contrary of that record`       IS FALSE
    `sterilisation`                                          IS st
    `has a sterilisation tattoo on its ear`                  IS FALSE
    `microchipping health certificate`                       IS NOTHING
    `sterilisation health certificate`                       IS NOTHING
    `is owned for the purpose of breeding`                   IS FALSE
    `in the custody of`                                      IS `anyone else` "its keeper"
    `foster care`                                            IS NOTHING

`kept by Ana since 1 Jan 2026` MEANS LIST `an individual` `Ana` (`the date` 2026 1 1)

-- Tom: born 1 January 2026, kept by Ana from birth, unregistered, unchipped, entire.
`Tom` MEANS `a cat` "Tom" (`the date` 2026 1 1) `kept by Ana since 1 Jan 2026` EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING

-- Tess: adult, chipped and desexed by a veterinarian, registered for one year from 1 March 2026.
`Tess` MEANS `a cat` "Tess" (`the date` 2020 6 1) `kept by Ana since 1 Jan 2026` (LIST `a registration with` "City of Perth" `in the name of` "Ana" `for` `one year` `from` (`the date` 2026 3 1)) (JUST (`a compliant chip implanted by` `Dr Vu` `on` (`the date` 2020 12 1))) (JUST (`a desexing by` `Dr Vu` `on` (`the date` 2020 12 1)))

-- Max: adult, chipped and desexed, unregistered, acquired by Ana on 1 March 2026.
`Max` MEANS `a cat` "Max" (`the date` 2020 6 1) (LIST `an individual` `Ana` (`the date` 2026 3 1)) EMPTY (JUST (`a compliant chip implanted by` `Dr Vu` `on` (`the date` 2020 12 1))) (JUST (`a desexing by` `Dr Vu` `on` (`the date` 2020 12 1)))

-- Mo: adult, kept by Kit (a child, Ana's) from 1 March 2026; unregistered.
`Mo` MEANS `a cat` "Mo" (`the date` 2020 6 1) (LIST `an individual` `Kit` (`the date` 2026 3 1)) EMPTY (JUST (`a compliant chip implanted by` `Dr Vu` `on` (`the date` 2020 12 1))) (JUST (`a desexing by` `Dr Vu` `on` (`the date` 2020 12 1)))

-- Biz: adult, kept by a cafe owned by Ben from 1 January 2026; unregistered.
`Biz` MEANS `a cat` "Biz" (`the date` 2020 6 1) (LIST `a business or organisation` "Cat Cafe Pty Ltd" (LIST `Ben`) (`the date` 2026 1 1)) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING

`Nia's cat` MEANS `a cat` "Nala" (`the date` 2020 6 1) (LIST `an individual` `Nia, newly arrived` (`the date` 2026 9 25)) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING
`Vic's cat` MEANS `a cat` "Vito" (`the date` 2020 6 1) (LIST `an individual` `Vic, not resident` (`the date` 2025 1 1)) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING

-- Chipped by Tech Lee, who holds a unit but no course: not a microchip implanter.
`Lee's cat` MEANS `a cat` "Lu" (`the date` 2020 6 1) `kept by Ana since 1 Jan 2026` EMPTY (JUST (`a compliant chip implanted by` `Tech Lee` `on` (`the date` 2026 2 1))) NOTHING

§ `Interpretation Act 1984 s 62 -- the Act's own examples`

#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 1 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2026 1 15) EQUALS `the date` 2026 2 14
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 1 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2026 1 30) EQUALS `the date` 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 1 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2026 1 31) EQUALS `the date` 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 1 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2028 1 31) EQUALS `the date` 2028 2 29
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 6 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2025 8 15) EQUALS `the date` 2026 2 14
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 6 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2025 8 30) EQUALS `the date` 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 6 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2025 8 31) EQUALS `the date` 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 6 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2027 8 31) EQUALS `the date` 2028 2 29
-- A period beginning on the 1st is the calendar months themselves.
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 1 `months beginning on` (`the date` 2026 2 1) EQUALS `the date` 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 3 `years beginning on` (`the date` 2023 1 10) EQUALS `the date` 2026 1 9

§ `Interpretation Act 1984 s 61 -- days`

-- 1 October 2026 is a Thursday; 3 October a Saturday.
#ASSERT `the weekday number of` (`the date` 2026 10 1) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 61(2) -- is an excluded day` (`the date` 2026 10 3) `given the holidays` `no holidays`
#ASSERT NOT `s 61(2) -- is an excluded day` (`the date` 2026 10 5) `given the holidays` `no holidays`
#ASSERT `s 61(2) -- is an excluded day` (`the date` 2026 12 25) `given the holidays` `the holidays`
-- Seven days after Friday 18 December 2026 ends on Friday 25 December, a holiday; then Saturday,
-- Sunday, and Monday 28 December, a holiday; so the thing may be done on Tuesday 29 December.
#ASSERT `s 61(1)(b) -- the last day of a period of` 7 `days after` (`the date` 2026 12 18) EQUALS `the date` 2026 12 25
#ASSERT `s 61 -- the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after` (`the date` 2026 12 18) `given the holidays` `the holidays` EQUALS `the date` 2026 12 29
#ASSERT `s 61 -- the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after` (`the date` 2026 10 1) `given the holidays` `the holidays` EQUALS `the date` 2026 10 8
#ASSERT `s 61(1)(a) -- the last day of a period of` 7 `days beginning on` (`the date` 2026 10 1) EQUALS `the date` 2026 10 7
#ASSERT `s 61(1)(g) -- the number of days between` (`the date` 2026 3 1) `and` (`the date` 2026 3 15) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `s 61(1)(f) -- the number of clear days between` (`the date` 2026 3 1) `and` (`the date` 2026 3 15) EQUALS 13

§ `Interpretation Act 1984 ss 71, 72`

#ASSERT `s 71(1)(d) -- on` (`the date` 2027 1 5) `the obligation still subsists, the period ending on` (`the date` 2026 12 29) `and the thing done on` NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 71(1)(d) -- on` (`the date` 2027 1 5) `the obligation still subsists, the period ending on` (`the date` 2026 12 29) `and the thing done on` (JUST (`the date` 2027 1 4))
#ASSERT NOT `s 71(1)(d) -- on` (`the date` 2026 12 29) `the obligation still subsists, the period ending on` (`the date` 2026 12 29) `and the thing done on` NOTHING
-- Convicted 1 March 2027, the thing done 11 March: a further offence for each of 2-10 March.
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the number of separate and further offences, convicted on` (`the date` 2027 3 1) `, done on` (JUST (`the date` 2027 3 11)) `, counted to` (`the date` 2027 4 1) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the number of separate and further offences, convicted on` (`the date` 2027 3 1) `, done on` NOTHING `, counted to` (`the date` 2027 3 4) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the number of separate and further offences, convicted on` (`the date` 2027 3 1) `, done on` (JUST (`the date` 2027 3 2)) `, counted to` (`the date` 2027 4 1) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the penalty for each separate and further offence` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 15 is` EQUALS "s 71(1)"
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 24 is` EQUALS "s 71(1)"
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 25 is` EQUALS "s 71(1)"
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 20 is` EQUALS "s 71(1)"
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 21 is` EQUALS "s 71(2)"
-- FORK-12, reading A (taken): s 71(2) reaches the "must ensure" duties.
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 5(1) is` EQUALS "s 71(2)"
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 14(1) is` EQUALS "s 71(2)"
#ASSERT `s 71 -- the subsection that applies to` `s 71 -- s 18(1) is` EQUALS "s 71(2)"
-- FORK-12, reading B: they are not duties "to do an act or thing", so s 71 does not reach them.
#ASSERT NOT `s 71, reading B of FORK-12 -- s 71 reaches the duty to ensure`

-- s 72: where the penalty sits decides which provision's contravention is the offence.
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- a contravention is an offence under` `s 5(1) -- penalty line`
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the provisions whose contravention is the offence under` `s 5(1) -- penalty line` EQUALS LIST "s 5(1)"
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the provisions whose contravention is the offence under` `s 7 -- penalty line` EQUALS LIST "s 7"
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the provisions whose contravention is the offence under` `s 23(2) -- penalty line` EQUALS LIST "s 23(2)"
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 24 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 6(1) -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 14(1) -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 15 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 16 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 17 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 18(1) -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 19 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 20 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 21 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 23(1) -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 72(1) -- the penalty on conviction under` `s 25 -- penalty line` EQUALS 5000

§ `Part 1 -- s 2 Commencement`

#ASSERT `s 2 -- the day` `s 5` `comes into operation, assent being on` (`the date` 2011 11 9) EQUALS `the date` 2013 11 1
#ASSERT `s 2 -- the day` `s 14(2)-(3)` `comes into operation, assent being on` (`the date` 2011 11 9) EQUALS `the date` 2012 11 1
#ASSERT `s 2 -- the day` `s 1` `comes into operation, assent being on` (`the date` 2011 11 9) EQUALS `the date` 2011 11 9
#ASSERT `s 2 -- the day` `s 24` `comes into operation, assent being on` (`the date` 2011 11 9) EQUALS `the date` 2013 11 1

§ `Part 1 -- age (FORK-01)`

`15 Aug 2025` MEANS `the date` 2025 8 15
`31 Aug 2025` MEANS `the date` 2025 8 31
`31 Aug 2027` MEANS `the date` 2027 8 31

-- Born 15 August 2025. Reading A (taken): 6 months of age on 15 February 2026.
#ASSERT NOT `15 Aug 2025` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2026 2 14)
#ASSERT `15 Aug 2025` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2026 2 15)
-- Reading B: on 16 February.
#ASSERT NOT `reading B --` `15 Aug 2025` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2026 2 15)
#ASSERT `reading B --` `15 Aug 2025` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2026 2 16)
-- Born 31 August: there is no 31 February, so the age is reached on 1 March on either reading.
#ASSERT NOT `31 Aug 2025` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `31 Aug 2025` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `reading B --` `31 Aug 2025` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2026 3 1)
-- ... and in a leap year, still not on 29 February.
#ASSERT NOT `31 Aug 2027` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `31 Aug 2027` `has reached` 6 `months of age on` (`the date` 2028 3 1)
-- Kit, born 10 March 2012, is a child until 9 March 2030 inclusive.
#ASSERT `Kit` `is a child under 18 years of age on` (`the date` 2030 3 9)
#ASSERT NOT `Kit` `is a child under 18 years of age on` (`the date` 2030 3 10)

§ `Part 1 -- s 3 Terms used`

`the council pound` MEANS `Facility` WITH
    `operator` IS "City of Perth", `is operated by a local government` IS TRUE
    `is, or may be, used for keeping cats` IS TRUE, `is a facility for keeping cats` IS TRUE
    `operator is approved in writing by a local government` IS FALSE

`the Cat Haven shelter` MEANS `Facility` WITH
    `operator` IS "Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven", `is operated by a local government` IS FALSE
    `is, or may be, used for keeping cats` IS TRUE, `is a facility for keeping cats` IS TRUE
    `operator is approved in writing by a local government` IS FALSE

`a private shelter` MEANS `Facility` WITH
    `operator` IS "Whiskers Rescue", `is operated by a local government` IS FALSE
    `is, or may be, used for keeping cats` IS TRUE, `is a facility for keeping cats` IS TRUE
    `operator is approved in writing by a local government` IS FALSE

`an approved private shelter` MEANS `Facility` WITH
    `operator` IS "Paws Rescue", `is operated by a local government` IS FALSE
    `is, or may be, used for keeping cats` IS TRUE, `is a facility for keeping cats` IS TRUE
    `operator is approved in writing by a local government` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a cat` `Tom`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a cat management facility` `the council pound`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a cat management facility` `the Cat Haven shelter`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a cat management facility` `an approved private shelter`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) -- is a cat management facility` `a private shelter`

#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` `Dr Vu`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` `Nurse Ng`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` `Tech Tan`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` `Tech Lee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` `Ana`

#ASSERT `s 3(1) --` `Tess` `is microchipped on` (`the date` 2026 10 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) --` `Tom` `is microchipped on` (`the date` 2026 10 1)
-- A working chip implanted by someone who is not a microchip implanter does not make the cat
-- "microchipped" (r 8).
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) --` `Lee's cat` `is microchipped on` (`the date` 2026 10 1)
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- is a microchip database company` `Petsafe`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) -- is a microchip database company` `an unlisted registry`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- there is a microchip database company for` `Tess`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) --` `Tess` `is sterilised on` (`the date` 2026 10 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) --` `Tom` `is sterilised on` (`the date` 2026 10 1)

-- "registered": Tess's one-year registration from 1 March 2026 runs to 31 October 2026.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) --` `Tess` `is registered on` (`the date` 2026 10 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) --` `Tess` `is registered on` (`the date` 2026 11 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(1) --` `Tess` `is registered on` (`the date` 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- the paragraph of "transfer" that covers` `reclaim from a cat management facility` EQUALS "(b)"
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- the paragraph of "transfer" that covers` `offer for sale` EQUALS "(a)"

§ `Part 1 -- s 4 Owner (FORK-02)`

-- A registered cat: the registered owner only, though Ana keeps her (the same person here).
#ASSERT `s 4 -- the owners of` `Tess` `on` (`the date` 2026 10 1) EQUALS LIST "Ana"
-- When her registration lapses, the keeper is the owner under (b).
